# RAPTOR — Research-Grade Radar Simulation Suite

RAPTOR is a self-contained C++17 radar simulation, signal-processing, imaging, tracking, and research-export workbench. It contains an analytical radar engine, a first-principles FDTD electromagnetic solver path, deterministic parallel random generation, optional OpenMP/MPI support, optional accelerator backends, and a broad command-line surface for radar phenomenology, RF impairments, clutter, electronic protection, target ingestion, MIMO/DOA processing, range-angle-Doppler products, truth scoring, Monte Carlo campaigns, and interoperability exports.

This README is source-derived for this release: it documents **all 342 command-line flags parsed by `src/raptor.cpp`**. CPU execution is the default; CUDA, ROCm/HIP, and Vulkan are optional build/runtime backends.

