## Accelerator backend model

The runtime backend selector is `--backend cpu|cuda|rocm|vulkan`. CPU is default and is always available. Accelerator flags only execute in binaries built with the matching backend compile definition. Backend verification compares accelerated products with CPU reference products using `--backend-tolerance`.

| Backend | Build switch | Runtime selector | Notes |
| - | - | - | - |
| CPU/OpenMP | default | `--backend cpu` | Dependency-free default path. |
| CUDA | `make CUDA=1` or `RAPTOR\_ENABLE\_CUDA=ON` | `--backend cuda`, `--cuda`, `--gpu` | NVIDIA CUDA path. Legacy flags preserved. |
| ROCm/HIP | `make ROCM=1` or `RAPTOR\_ENABLE\_ROCM=ON` | `--backend rocm`, `--rocm`, `--hip` | AMD HIP kernel path. |
| Vulkan compute | `make VULKAN=1` or `RAPTOR\_ENABLE\_VULKAN=ON` | `--backend vulkan`, `--vulkan` | Vulkan compute path requiring Vulkan and shaderc. |


