## Implementation notes and limitations

- The default build is intentionally dependency-free and uses a built-in radix-2 FFT. FFT sizes are validated and rounded to a power of two when needed.

- The analytical engine is a research simulation model, not a certified radar design tool. It emphasizes reproducible algorithm experimentation and comparative studies.

- Several research flags select lightweight internal models rather than external packages; outputs are explicit so results can be inspected and validated externally.

- Accelerator support is optional. CPU remains the canonical reference path; `--backend-verify` is intended for accelerator/CPU product comparisons.

- The FDTD solver is separate from the analytical imaging engine and is selected with `--solver fdtd`.

- Scenario parsing supports a practical YAML/JSON subset without external dependencies; it is not a full YAML 1.2 parser.

- MATLAB export uses a dependency-free MATLAB v4-style image output path; NumPy export writes `.npy`-style array products where implemented.

